# `git blame` would otherwise name these as the last change to most lines in the
# repo, which makes it useless for the question people actually ask it. GitHub reads
# this file automatically; locally it needs
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# which `composer hooks:install` sets up.
#
# Only whitespace, import and docblock-type commits belong here. A commit that
# changed behaviour must never be added, however mechanical it looked.

